{
 "unidades": [
  {
   "id": "u08",
   "titulo": {"es": "Nasales II: in, un", "en": "Nasal vowels II: in, un"},
   "objetivo": {"es": "Leer la nasal in (in, ain, ein, im, un), distinguirla de on y an, y saber cuándo la n vuelve a sonar: bon/bonne, un/une.", "en": "Read the nasal in (in, ain, ein, im, un), tell it apart from on and an, and know when the n comes back: bon/bonne, un/une."},
   "lecciones": [
    {
     "id": "u08.l01",
     "titulo": {"es": "in, ain, ein", "en": "in, ain, ein"},
     "pasos": [
      {"tipo": "lumo", "pose": "anima", "texto": {"es": "Tercera nasal: la in de lapin (conejo). Sonríe un poco, di una «e» abierta y deja salir el aire por la nariz.", "en": "Third nasal vowel: the in of lapin (rabbit). Smile a little, say the e in bed and let the air out through your nose."}},
      {"tipo": "mira", "m": "l(a:a)p(in:in)", "sonido": "in", "texto": {"es": "In no se lee como el «in» del español: es una sola vocal nasal y la n no suena.", "en": "In isn't read like English “in”: it's a single nasal vowel, and the n is silent."}},
      {"tipo": "escucha", "palabras": [{"m": "l(a:a)p(in:in)", "e": "1f430", "t": {"es": "conejo", "en": "rabbit"}}, {"m": "p(ain:in)", "e": "1f35e", "t": {"es": "pan", "en": "bread"}}, {"m": "v(in:in)", "e": "1f377", "t": {"es": "vino", "en": "wine"}}, {"m": "m(ain:in)", "e": "270b", "t": {"es": "mano", "en": "hand"}}]},
      {"tipo": "mira", "m": "p(ain:in)", "sonido": "in", "texto": {"es": "Ain y ein suenan igual que in: pain (pan), plein (lleno). Tres grafías, un solo sonido.", "en": "Ain and ein sound just like in: pain (bread), plein (full). Three spellings, one sound."}},
      {"tipo": "escucha", "palabras": [{"m": "tr(ain:in)", "e": "1f686", "t": {"es": "tren", "en": "train"}}, {"m": "pl(ein:in)", "t": {"es": "lleno", "en": "full"}}, {"m": "j(a:a)rd(in:in)", "t": {"es": "jardín", "en": "garden"}}, {"m": "s(a:a)p(in:in)", "e": "1f332", "t": {"es": "abeto (árbol de Navidad)", "en": "fir tree"}}]},
      {"tipo": "mezcla", "m": "j(a:a)rd(in:in)", "t": {"es": "jardín", "en": "garden"}},
      {"tipo": "toca_sonido", "sonido": "in", "pregunta": {"es": "¿Cuál tiene la in de lapin?", "en": "Which one has the in in lapin?"}, "opciones": [{"m": "b(on:on)"}, {"m": "m(ain:in)", "e": "270b"}, {"m": "l(ou:ou)(p:_)", "e": "1f43a"}], "correcta": 1},
      {"tipo": "escucha_elige", "audio": "vin", "pregunta": {"es": "¿vie o vin?", "en": "vie or vin?"}, "opciones": [{"m": "v(i:i)(e:_)"}, {"m": "v(in:in)"}], "correcta": 1},
      {"tipo": "cambia", "de": "p(ain:in)", "a": "m(ain:in)", "opciones": ["p", "m", "b"]},
      {"tipo": "repite", "m": "l(a:a)p(in:in)", "t": {"es": "conejo", "en": "rabbit"}}
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "u08.l02",
     "titulo": {"es": "un, im", "en": "un, im"},
     "pasos": [
      {"tipo": "mira", "m": "l(un:in)d(i:i)", "sonido": "in", "texto": {"es": "En el francés de Francia, un suena igual que in: lundi (lunes), un (uno).", "en": "In standard French from France, un sounds just like in: lundi (Monday), un (one)."}},
      {"tipo": "escucha", "palabras": [{"m": "(un:in)", "t": {"es": "un, uno", "en": "a, one"}}, {"m": "l(un:in)d(i:i)", "t": {"es": "lunes", "en": "Monday"}}, {"m": "br(un:in)", "t": {"es": "castaño", "en": "brown"}}, {"m": "(au:o)c(un:in)", "t": {"es": "ninguno", "en": "none"}}]},
      {"tipo": "lumo", "pose": "pensando", "texto": {"es": "Ojo: al final no subas la lengua al paladar. Si se oye una n clara, ya no es nasal.", "en": "Careful: at the end, don't lift your tongue to the roof of your mouth. If you hear a clear n, it's no longer nasal."}},
      {"tipo": "mira", "m": "s(im:in)pl(e:_)", "sonido": "in", "texto": {"es": "Antes de p o b, la n se escribe m: im, como en simple. Suena igual que in.", "en": "Before p or b, the n is written m: im, as in simple. It sounds just like in."}},
      {"tipo": "escucha", "palabras": [{"m": "s(im:in)pl(e:_)", "t": {"es": "simple", "en": "simple"}}, {"m": "t(im:in)br(e:_)", "t": {"es": "sello (de correo)", "en": "stamp"}}, {"m": "(im:in)p(o:oo)(ss:=)(i:i)bl(e:_)", "t": {"es": "imposible", "en": "impossible"}}, {"m": "gr(im:in)p(er:e)", "t": {"es": "trepar", "en": "to climb"}}]},
      {"tipo": "mezcla", "m": "l(un:in)d(i:i)", "t": {"es": "lunes", "en": "Monday"}},
      {"tipo": "toca_sonido", "sonido": "in", "pregunta": {"es": "¿Cuál tiene la in de lapin?", "en": "Which one has the in in lapin?"}, "opciones": [{"m": "br(un:in)"}, {"m": "b(u:u)s", "e": "1f68c"}, {"m": "l(u:u)n(e:_)", "e": "1f319"}], "correcta": 0},
      {"tipo": "elige_significado", "m": "l(un:in)d(i:i)", "pregunta": {"es": "¿Qué significa?", "en": "What does it mean?"}, "opciones": [{"es": "lunes", "en": "Monday"}, {"es": "luna", "en": "moon"}, {"es": "domingo", "en": "Sunday"}], "correcta": 0},
      {"tipo": "lee", "m": "L(un:in)d(i:i), j(e:schwa) m(an:an)g(e:_) d(u:u) p(ain:in).", "t": {"es": "El lunes como pan.", "en": "On Monday I eat bread."}, "pregunta": {"es": "¿Qué como el lunes?", "en": "What do I eat on Monday?"}, "opciones": [{"e": "1f35e"}, {"e": "1f34e"}], "correcta": 0},
      {"tipo": "repite", "m": "br(un:in)", "t": {"es": "castaño", "en": "brown"}}
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "u08.l03",
     "titulo": {"es": "on, an, in", "en": "on, an, in"},
     "pasos": [
      {"tipo": "lumo", "pose": "escucha", "texto": {"es": "Ya conoces tres nasales: on, an, in. Cambia la boca: redonda para on, abierta para an, sonriente para in.", "en": "You now know three nasal vowels: on, an, in. Change your mouth: round for on, open for an, smiling for in."}},
      {"tipo": "escucha", "palabras": [{"m": "b(on:on)", "t": {"es": "bueno", "en": "good"}}, {"m": "b(an:an)(c:_)", "t": {"es": "banco (para sentarse)", "en": "bench"}}, {"m": "b(ain:in)", "e": "1f6c1", "t": {"es": "baño (en la tina)", "en": "bath"}}]},
      {"tipo": "escucha_elige", "audio": "bain", "pregunta": {"es": "¿bon, banc o bain?", "en": "bon, banc or bain?"}, "opciones": [{"m": "b(on:on)"}, {"m": "b(an:an)(c:_)"}, {"m": "b(ain:in)"}], "correcta": 2},
      {"tipo": "escucha", "palabras": [{"m": "l(on:on)(g:_)", "t": {"es": "largo", "en": "long"}}, {"m": "l(en:an)(t:_)", "t": {"es": "lento", "en": "slow"}}, {"m": "l(in:in)", "t": {"es": "lino", "en": "linen"}}]},
      {"tipo": "escucha_elige", "audio": "lent", "pregunta": {"es": "¿long, lent o lin?", "en": "long, lent or lin?"}, "opciones": [{"m": "l(on:on)(g:_)"}, {"m": "l(en:an)(t:_)"}, {"m": "l(in:in)"}], "correcta": 1},
      {"tipo": "escucha_elige", "audio": "vin", "pregunta": {"es": "¿vont, vent o vin?", "en": "vont, vent or vin?"}, "opciones": [{"m": "v(on:on)(t:_)"}, {"m": "v(en:an)(t:_)"}, {"m": "v(in:in)"}], "correcta": 2},
      {"tipo": "escucha_elige", "audio": "son", "pregunta": {"es": "¿son, sans o saint?", "en": "son, sans or saint?"}, "opciones": [{"m": "s(on:on)"}, {"m": "s(an:an)(s:_)"}, {"m": "s(ain:in)(t:_)"}], "correcta": 0},
      {"tipo": "toca_sonido", "sonido": "an", "pregunta": {"es": "¿Cuál tiene la an de dent?", "en": "Which one has the an in dent?"}, "opciones": [{"m": "l(on:on)(g:_)"}, {"m": "l(en:an)(t:_)"}, {"m": "l(in:in)"}], "correcta": 1},
      {"tipo": "toca_sonido", "sonido": "in", "pregunta": {"es": "¿Cuál tiene la in de lapin?", "en": "Which one has the in in lapin?"}, "opciones": [{"m": "m(on:on)"}, {"m": "m(ain:in)", "e": "270b"}, {"m": "m(a:a)m(an:an)"}], "correcta": 1},
      {"tipo": "repite", "m": "b(ain:in)", "t": {"es": "baño", "en": "bath"}}
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "u08.l04",
     "titulo": {"es": "bon, bonne", "en": "bon, bonne"},
     "pasos": [
      {"tipo": "lumo", "pose": "sorprendido", "texto": {"es": "Si después de la n viene una vocal u otra n, la nasal desaparece y la n sí suena. Bon (bueno) → bonne (buena).", "en": "If a vowel or another n follows the n, the nasal disappears and you hear the n. Bon (good, masc.) → bonne (good, fem.)."}},
      {"tipo": "mira", "m": "b(o:oo)nn(e:_)", "sonido": "oo", "texto": {"es": "En bonne, la o es oral, como en pomme, y luego suena la n. La e final no suena.", "en": "In bonne, the o is oral, as in pomme, and then you hear the n. The final e is silent."}},
      {"tipo": "escucha", "palabras": [{"m": "b(on:on)", "t": {"es": "bueno", "en": "good (masc.)"}}, {"m": "b(o:oo)nn(e:_)", "t": {"es": "buena", "en": "good (fem.)"}}, {"m": "(un:in)", "t": {"es": "un, uno", "en": "a, one (masc.)"}}, {"m": "(u:u)n(e:_)", "t": {"es": "una", "en": "a, one (fem.)"}}]},
      {"tipo": "escucha", "palabras": [{"m": "c(ou:ou)s(in:in)", "t": {"es": "primo", "en": "cousin (male)"}}, {"m": "c(ou:ou)s(i:i)n(e:_)", "t": {"es": "prima", "en": "cousin (female)"}}, {"m": "pl(ein:in)", "t": {"es": "lleno", "en": "full (masc.)"}}, {"m": "pl(ei:eh)n(e:_)", "t": {"es": "llena", "en": "full (fem.)"}}]},
      {"tipo": "escucha_elige", "audio": "bonne", "pregunta": {"es": "¿bon o bonne?", "en": "bon or bonne?"}, "opciones": [{"m": "b(on:on)"}, {"m": "b(o:oo)nn(e:_)"}], "correcta": 1},
      {"tipo": "escucha_elige", "audio": "un", "pregunta": {"es": "¿un o une?", "en": "un or une?"}, "opciones": [{"m": "(un:in)"}, {"m": "(u:u)n(e:_)"}], "correcta": 0},
      {"tipo": "escucha_elige", "audio": "américaine", "pregunta": {"es": "¿américain o américaine?", "en": "américain or américaine?"}, "opciones": [{"m": "(a:a)m(é:e)r(i:i)c(ain:in)"}, {"m": "(a:a)m(é:e)r(i:i)c(ai:eh)n(e:_)"}], "correcta": 1},
      {"tipo": "construye", "m": "c(ou:ou)s(i:i)n(e:_)", "fichas": ["c", "o", "u", "s", "i", "n", "e", "a"]},
      {"tipo": "lee", "m": "M(a:a) c(ou:ou)s(i:i)n(e:_) (e:eh)(st:_) (a:a)m(é:e)r(i:i)c(ai:eh)n(e:_).", "t": {"es": "Mi prima es estadounidense.", "en": "My cousin is American."}, "pregunta": {"es": "¿Quién es estadounidense?", "en": "Who is American?"}, "opciones": [{"m": "c(ou:ou)s(in:in)"}, {"m": "c(ou:ou)s(i:i)n(e:_)"}], "correcta": 1},
      {"tipo": "lumo", "pose": "celebra", "texto": {"es": "¡Ya lees las tres nasales! Y sabes cuándo la n vuelve a sonar.", "en": "You can read all three nasal vowels! And you know when the n comes back."}}
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "u09",
   "titulo": {"es": "gn, ill, la R y -ent", "en": "gn, ill, the R and -ent"},
   "objetivo": {"es": "Leer gn (como la ñ) e ill (como la y de «hoy»), decir la R francesa y saber que -ent no suena en los verbos.", "en": "Read gn (like ny in canyon) and ill (like y in yes), say the French R, and know that verb -ent is silent."},
   "lecciones": [
    {
     "id": "u09.l01",
     "titulo": {"es": "gn = ñ", "en": "gn = ny"},
     "pasos": [
      {"tipo": "lumo", "pose": "anima", "texto": {"es": "Buena noticia: gn suena como la ñ del español. Ya sabes decirlo.", "en": "Good news: gn sounds like the ny in canyon. You already know this sound."}},
      {"tipo": "mira", "m": "m(on:on)t(a:a)(gn:=)(e:_)", "texto": {"es": "Dos letras, un sonido: gn = ñ. Montagne significa montaña.", "en": "Two letters, one sound: gn = ny. Montagne means mountain."}},
      {"tipo": "escucha", "palabras": [{"m": "m(on:on)t(a:a)(gn:=)(e:_)", "e": "26f0", "t": {"es": "montaña", "en": "mountain"}}, {"m": "(ch:=)(am:an)p(i:i)(gn:=)(on:on)", "e": "1f344", "t": {"es": "hongo, champiñón", "en": "mushroom"}}, {"m": "(a:a)(gn:=)(eau:o)", "e": "1f411", "t": {"es": "cordero", "en": "lamb"}}, {"m": "c(y:i)(gn:=)(e:_)", "e": "1f9a2", "t": {"es": "cisne", "en": "swan"}}]},
      {"tipo": "mezcla", "m": "(E:eh)sp(a:a)(gn:=)(e:_)", "t": {"es": "España", "en": "Spain"}},
      {"tipo": "escucha_elige", "audio": "agneau", "pregunta": {"es": "¿agneau o anneau?", "en": "agneau or anneau?"}, "opciones": [{"m": "(a:a)(gn:=)(eau:o)", "e": "1f411"}, {"m": "(a:a)nn(eau:o)", "e": "1f48d"}], "correcta": 0},
      {"tipo": "escucha_elige", "audio": "champion", "pregunta": {"es": "¿champignon o champion?", "en": "champignon or champion?"}, "opciones": [{"m": "(ch:=)(am:an)p(i:i)(gn:=)(on:on)"}, {"m": "(ch:=)(am:an)p(i:i)(on:on)"}], "correcta": 1},
      {"tipo": "elige_significado", "m": "m(on:on)t(a:a)(gn:=)(e:_)", "pregunta": {"es": "¿Qué significa?", "en": "What does it mean?"}, "opciones": [{"es": "montaña", "en": "mountain"}, {"es": "mantequilla", "en": "butter"}, {"es": "moneda", "en": "coin"}], "correcta": 0},
      {"tipo": "construye", "m": "s(i:i)(gn:=)(e:_)", "fichas": ["s", "i", "g", "n", "e", "o"]},
      {"tipo": "cambia", "de": "l(i:i)(gn:=)(e:_)", "a": "s(i:i)(gn:=)(e:_)", "opciones": ["l", "s", "v"]},
      {"tipo": "repite", "m": "(a:a)(gn:=)(eau:o)", "t": {"es": "cordero", "en": "lamb"}}
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "u09.l02",
     "titulo": {"es": "ill = y", "en": "ill = y"},
     "pasos": [
      {"tipo": "mira", "m": "f(i:i)(ll:=)(e:_)", "texto": {"es": "Después de i, ll suele sonar como la y de «hoy»: fille (hija, chica).", "en": "After i, ll usually sounds like the y in yes: fille (daughter, girl)."}},
      {"tipo": "escucha", "palabras": [{"m": "f(i:i)(ll:=)(e:_)", "e": "1f467", "t": {"es": "hija, chica", "en": "daughter, girl"}}, {"m": "f(a:a)m(i:i)(ll:=)(e:_)", "e": "1f46a", "t": {"es": "familia", "en": "family"}}, {"m": "(a:a)b(e:eh)(ill:=)(e:_)", "e": "1f41d", "t": {"es": "abeja", "en": "bee"}}, {"m": "gr(e:schwa)n(ou:ou)(ill:=)(e:_)", "e": "1f438", "t": {"es": "rana", "en": "frog"}}]},
      {"tipo": "mira", "m": "s(o:oo)l(e:eh)(il:=)", "texto": {"es": "Al final de palabra, -il después de vocal también suena y: soleil (sol), travail (trabajo).", "en": "At the end of a word, -il after a vowel also sounds like y: soleil (sun), travail (work)."}},
      {"tipo": "escucha", "palabras": [{"m": "s(o:oo)l(e:eh)(il:=)", "e": "2600", "t": {"es": "sol", "en": "sun"}}, {"m": "tr(a:a)v(a:a)(il:=)", "t": {"es": "trabajo", "en": "work"}}, {"m": "f(eu:oeu)(ill:=)(e:_)", "e": "1f343", "t": {"es": "hoja (de árbol)", "en": "leaf"}}, {"m": "r(é:e)v(e:eh)(il:=)", "e": "23f0", "t": {"es": "despertador", "en": "alarm clock"}}]},
      {"tipo": "lumo", "pose": "pensando", "texto": {"es": "Excepciones: ville (ciudad), mille (mil) y tranquille. Ahí ll suena l.", "en": "Exceptions: ville (city), mille (thousand) and tranquille. There ll sounds like l."}},
      {"tipo": "mezcla", "m": "f(a:a)m(i:i)(ll:=)(e:_)", "t": {"es": "familia", "en": "family"}},
      {"tipo": "escucha_elige", "audio": "fille", "pregunta": {"es": "¿fil o fille?", "en": "fil or fille?"}, "opciones": [{"m": "f(i:i)l"}, {"m": "f(i:i)(ll:=)(e:_)"}], "correcta": 1},
      {"tipo": "escucha_elige", "audio": "ville", "pregunta": {"es": "¿ville o fille?", "en": "ville or fille?"}, "opciones": [{"m": "v(i:i)ll(e:_)"}, {"m": "f(i:i)(ll:=)(e:_)"}], "correcta": 0},
      {"tipo": "construye", "m": "s(o:oo)l(e:eh)(il:=)", "fichas": ["s", "o", "l", "e", "i", "l", "a"]},
      {"tipo": "repite", "m": "(a:a)b(e:eh)(ill:=)(e:_)", "t": {"es": "abeja", "en": "bee"}}
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "u09.l03",
     "titulo": {"es": "La R francesa", "en": "The French R"},
     "pasos": [
      {"tipo": "lumo", "pose": "pensando", "texto": {"es": "La r francesa no vibra como la rr. Se hace atrás, en la garganta: es como una «j» suave, pero con voz.", "en": "The French r doesn't roll. It's made at the back of the throat, a bit like a soft gargle."}},
      {"tipo": "mira", "m": "r(ou:ou)g(e:_)", "texto": {"es": "Rouge (rojo): deja la punta de la lengua abajo, detrás de los dientes, y haz la r atrás.", "en": "Rouge (red): keep the tip of your tongue down behind your teeth and make the r at the back."}},
      {"tipo": "escucha", "palabras": [{"m": "r(ou:ou)g(e:_)", "e": "1f534", "t": {"es": "rojo", "en": "red"}}, {"m": "r(u:u)(e:_)", "t": {"es": "calle", "en": "street"}}, {"m": "P(a:a)r(i:i)(s:_)", "t": {"es": "París", "en": "Paris"}}, {"m": "m(e:eh)rc(i:i)", "e": "1f64f", "t": {"es": "gracias", "en": "thank you"}}]},
      {"tipo": "mezcla", "m": "m(e:eh)rc(i:i)", "t": {"es": "gracias", "en": "thank you"}},
      {"tipo": "escucha_elige", "audio": "riz", "pregunta": {"es": "¿riz o lit?", "en": "riz or lit?"}, "opciones": [{"m": "r(i:i)(z:_)", "e": "1f35a"}, {"m": "l(i:i)(t:_)", "e": "1f6cf"}], "correcta": 0},
      {"tipo": "escucha_elige", "audio": "rat", "pregunta": {"es": "¿chat o rat?", "en": "chat or rat?"}, "opciones": [{"m": "(ch:=)(a:a)(t:_)", "e": "1f431"}, {"m": "r(a:a)(t:_)", "e": "1f400"}], "correcta": 1},
      {"tipo": "escucha", "palabras": [{"m": "fr(è:eh)r(e:_)", "t": {"es": "hermano", "en": "brother"}}, {"m": "m(è:eh)r(e:_)", "t": {"es": "madre", "en": "mother"}}, {"m": "p(o:oo)rt(e:_)", "e": "1f6aa", "t": {"es": "puerta", "en": "door"}}, {"m": "fl(eu:oeu)r", "e": "1f338", "t": {"es": "flor", "en": "flower"}}]},
      {"tipo": "elige_significado", "m": "fr(è:eh)r(e:_)", "pregunta": {"es": "¿Qué significa?", "en": "What does it mean?"}, "opciones": [{"es": "hermano", "en": "brother"}, {"es": "padre", "en": "father"}, {"es": "fresa", "en": "strawberry"}], "correcta": 0},
      {"tipo": "construye", "m": "r(ou:ou)g(e:_)", "fichas": ["r", "o", "u", "g", "e", "a"]},
      {"tipo": "repite", "m": "P(a:a)r(i:i)(s:_)", "t": {"es": "París", "en": "Paris"}}
     ]
    },
    {
     "id": "u09.l04",
     "titulo": {"es": "ils parlent", "en": "ils parlent"},
     "pasos": [
      {"tipo": "lumo", "pose": "sorprendido", "texto": {"es": "Sorpresa: en los verbos, -ent al final no suena. Il parle (él habla) e ils parlent (ellos hablan) se oyen igual.", "en": "Surprise: in verbs, a final -ent is silent. Il parle (he speaks) and ils parlent (they speak) sound the same."}},
      {"tipo": "mira", "m": "p(a:a)rl(ent:_)", "texto": {"es": "Las tres letras -ent de parlent son mudas, igual que la s de ils.", "en": "The three letters -ent in parlent are silent, just like the s in ils."}},
      {"tipo": "escucha", "palabras": [{"m": "(i:i)l p(a:a)rl(e:_)", "t": {"es": "él habla", "en": "he speaks"}}, {"m": "(i:i)l(s:_) p(a:a)rl(ent:_)", "t": {"es": "ellos hablan", "en": "they speak"}}, {"m": "(e:eh)ll(e:_) (ch:=)(an:an)t(e:_)", "t": {"es": "ella canta", "en": "she sings"}}, {"m": "(e:eh)ll(es:_) (ch:=)(an:an)t(ent:_)", "t": {"es": "ellas cantan", "en": "they sing (fem.)"}}]},
      {"tipo": "elige_significado", "m": "(e:eh)ll(es:_) d(an:an)s(ent:_)", "pregunta": {"es": "¿Qué significa?", "en": "What does it mean?"}, "opciones": [{"es": "ellas bailan", "en": "they dance"}, {"es": "ella baila", "en": "she dances"}, {"es": "ellas cantan", "en": "they sing"}], "correcta": 0},
      {"tipo": "lumo", "pose": "pensando", "texto": {"es": "Ojo: solo en los verbos. En le vent (el viento) o lent (lento), en sí suena: es la an de dent.", "en": "Careful: only in verbs. In le vent (the wind) or lent (slow), en is pronounced: it's the an in dent."}},
      {"tipo": "toca_sonido", "sonido": "an", "pregunta": {"es": "¿Cuál tiene la an de dent?", "en": "Which one has the an in dent?"}, "opciones": [{"m": "p(a:a)rl(ent:_)"}, {"m": "v(en:an)(t:_)"}, {"m": "(ai:eh)m(ent:_)"}], "correcta": 1},
      {"tipo": "construye", "m": "p(a:a)rl(ent:_)", "fichas": ["p", "a", "r", "l", "e", "n", "t", "o"]},
      {"tipo": "lee", "m": "(E:eh)ll(es:_) r(e:schwa)g(a:a)rd(ent:_) l(a:a) l(u:u)n(e:_).", "t": {"es": "Ellas miran la luna.", "en": "They are looking at the moon."}, "pregunta": {"es": "¿Qué miran?", "en": "What are they looking at?"}, "opciones": [{"e": "1f319"}, {"e": "2600"}], "correcta": 0},
      {"tipo": "lee", "m": "L(es:e) f(i:i)(ll:=)(es:_) (ch:=)(an:an)t(ent:_) d(an:an)(s:_) l(e:schwa) j(a:a)rd(in:in).", "t": {"es": "Las chicas cantan en el jardín.", "en": "The girls sing in the garden."}, "pregunta": {"es": "¿Qué hacen las chicas?", "en": "What are the girls doing?"}, "opciones": [{"e": "1f3a4"}, {"e": "1f634"}], "correcta": 0},
      {"tipo": "repite", "m": "(i:i)l(s:_) p(a:a)rl(ent:_)", "t": {"es": "ellos hablan", "en": "they speak"}}
